rmula: p2 - (l1 - overlap) = 4 - (3-1) = 2 ✓\n//   And l2' = l2 - overlap = 3 - 1 = 2 ✓\n\n// Case 6: p2 < p1 and p2_end < p1_end and p2_end > p1  → partial overlap, op2 extends into op1's start\n//   Symmetric to case 5\n\nLet me enumerate all cases clearly for delete-delete transform:\n\nCase A: e1 <= p2 — op1 entirely before op2, no overlap\n  op1' = op1\n  op2' = delete(p2 - l1, l2)\n\nCase B: e2 <= p1 — op2 entirely before op1, no overlap\n  op1' = delete(p1 - l2, l1)\n  op2' = op2\n\nCase C: p1 <= p2 and e1 >= e2 — op1 contains op2\n  op1' = delete(p1, l1 - l2)\n  op2' = op2\n\nCase D: p2 <= p1 and e2 >= e1 — op2 contains op1\n  op1' = null  // op2 removes everything op1 does\n  op2' = delete(p2, l2 - l1)\n\nCase E: p1 < p2 and p2 < e1 and e1 < e2 — op1 overlaps left part of op2\n  overlap = e1 - p2\n  op1' = delete(p1, l1 - overlap)\n  op2' = delete(p2 - (l1 - overlap), l2 - overlap)\n  \n  // Wait, is this right? Let me verify with the earlier example.\n  op1 = delete(2, 3), op2 = delete(4, 3)\n  Case E: p1=2 < p2=4 ✓, p2=4 < e1=5 ✓, e1=5 < e2=7 ✓\n  overlap = 1\n  op1' = delete(2, 2) ✓\n  op2' = delete(4 - 2, 2) = delete(2, 2) ✓\n  \n  Let's verify convergence:\n  Apply S=\"HelloWorld\", op1=delete(2,3) → \"HeWorld\", op2'=delete(2,2) → \"Held\"\n  Apply S=\"HelloWorld\", op2=delete(4,3) → \"Hellrld\", op1'=delete(2,2) → \"Held\" ✓✓✓\n\nCase F: p2 < p1 and p1 < e2 and e2 < e1 — op2 overlaps left part of op1\n  overlap = e2 - p1\n  op1' = delete(p1 - (l2 - overlap), l1 - overlap)\n  op2' = delete(p2, l2 - overlap)\n  \n  Verify: op1 = delete(4, 3), op2 = delete(2, 3)\n  S = \"HelloWorld\", op1 = delete(4,3) → \"Hellrld\", op2 = delete(2,3) → \"HeWorld\"\n  Case F: p2=2 < p1=4 ✓, p1=4 < e2=5 ✓, e2=5 < e1=7 ✓\n  overlap = 5 - 4 = 1\n  op1' = delete(4 - 2, 2) = delete(2, 2)  ✓  (removes \"rl\" → wait, after op2 deletes \"llo\" from \"HelloWorld\", it becomes \"HeWorld\", then op1'=delete(2,2) removes \"Wo\" → \"Held\"... hmm that doesn't match)\n  \n  Let me re