+{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"a66980e5-0367-4805-9af9-3964a3f58e58","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_00_NBdcEnozeTndKgWHtwlb1141","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/CONTRACT.md","content":"# Contract: Real-Time Collaborative Document Editor\n\n## 1. OT Module (`src/ot.ts`)\n\n### 1.1 Operation Types\n- [x] Insert operation: `{ type: 'insert', pos: number, text: string, clientId: string }`\n- [x] Delete operation: `{ type: 'delete', pos: number, length: number, clientId: string }`\n- [x] `applyOperation(content: string, op: Operation): string` applies an insert or delete to a string\n- [x] `applyOperation` works on empty string\n- [x] `applyOperation` rejects insert at position > content length\n- [x] `applyOperation` rejects delete extending past content length\n\n### 1.2 Transform: insert vs insert\n- [x] Two inserts at different positions: both preserved, later insert position adjusted\n- [x] Two inserts at same position: determined by clientId ordering, second shifted\n\n### 1.3 Transform: insert vs delete\n- [x] Insert before delete: delete position shifts by insert length\n- [x] Insert after delete: insert position shifts by delete length\n- [x] Insert at same position as delete start: insert first, shift delete position\n\n### 1.4 Transform: delete vs delete (no overlap)\n- [x] Delete entirely before other: positions unaffected for first, second shifts\n- [x] Delete entirely after other: first shifts, second unaffected\n\n### 1.5 Transform: delete vs delete (overlap)\n- [x] One contains the other: contained becomes no-op, container shrinks\n- [x] Partial overlap: both lengths reduce by overlap amount, positions adjust\n- [x] Identical deletes: both become no-ops\n\n### 1.6 Transform: convergence property\n- [x] `apply(apply(S, op1), transform(op2, op1)[1])` === `apply(apply(S, op2), transform(op1, op2)[1])`\n- [x] This holds for all operation combinations\n- [x] `transform(op1, op2)` returns `[op1_prime, op2_prime]`\n\n## 2. Database Layer (`src/db.ts`)\n\n### 2.1 Initialization\n- [x] Opens/create SQLite database at given path\n- [x] Runs schema from schema.sql\n- [x] Tables exist: documents, versions, active_connections\n\n### 2.2 Document CRUD\n- [x] `createDocument(title)`: returns doc with id, title, content='', timestamps\n- [x] `getDocument(id)`: returns document or null if not found\n- [x] `listDocuments()`: returns array of all documents\n- [x] `updateDocument(id, title, content)`: updates fields and updated_at\n- [x] `deleteDocument(id)`: removes document and cascade deletes versions/connections\n\n### 2.3 Version History\n- [x] `addVersion(docId, version, content, operation)`: stores a version snapshot\n- [x] `getVersions(docId)`: returns ordered version list\n- [x] `getLatestVersion(docId)`: returns latest version number or 0\n\n### 2.4 Active Connections\n- [x] `addConnection(id, docId)`: records active connection\n- [x] `removeConnection(id)`: removes connection\n- [x] `getConnectionCount(docId)`: returns connection count for a document\n\n## 3. REST API\n\n### 3.1 Create Document\n- [x] `POST /api/documents` with `{ title }` → 201 + document object\n- [x] Rejects missing title with 400\n\n### 3.2 List Documents\n- [x] `GET /api/documents` → 200 + array of documents\n\n### 3.3 Get Document\n- [x] `GET /api/documents/:id` → 200 + document object\n- [x] Returns 404 for non-existent document\n\n### 3.4 Update Document\n- [x] `PUT /api/documents/:id` with `{ title?, content? }` → 200 + updated document\n- [x] Returns 404 for non-existent document\n\n### 3.5 Delete Document\n- [x] `DELETE /api/documents/:id` → 204\n- [x] Returns 404 for non-existent document\n\n### 3.6 Version History\n- [x] `GET /api/documents/:id/versions` → 200 + version array\n- [x] Returns 404 for non-existent document\n\n## 4. WebSocket & Real-Time Collaboration\n\n### 4.1 Connection\n- [x] Connect to `ws://host/document/:docId`\n- [x] Server sends `{ type: 'sync', content: string, version: number }` on connect\n\n### 4.2 Receiving Edits\n- [x] Client sends `{ type: 'operation', op: Operation, version: number }`\n- [x] Server validates operation (insert within bounds, delete within bounds)\n- [x] Server rejects invalid operations with `{ type: 'error', message }`\n- [x] Server applies operation, increments version, stores version\n- [x] Server broadcasts operation to all OTHER clients on same document\n\n### 4.3 Broadcasting\n- [x] Broadcast message: `{ type: 'operation', op: Operation, version: number, clientId: string }`\n- [x] Sender does NOT receive their own broadcast\n- [x] Different documents are isolated — edits on doc A don't reach doc B clients\n\n### 4.4 OT (Server-side)\n- [x] If a client's operation has a stale version (server has advanced), server transforms it through intervening ops\n- [x] Transformed operation is applied and broadcast\n\n### 4.5 Disconnection\n- [x] Removing a connection record on WebSocket close\n\n## 5. Server Factory (`createApp`)\n\n### 5.1 Factory\n- [x] `createApp(dbPath?)` returns `{ app, start, stop }`\n- [x] `app` is the Express application\n- [x] `start(port?)` starts listening, returns port number (port 0 = random)\n- [x] `stop()` shuts down server, closes all WebSocket connections, closes database\n- [x] If no dbPath given, uses `:memory:` for in-memory database\n\n## 6. Full Integration\n\n### 6.1 Full lifecycle\n- [x] Create doc via REST → connect via WS → receive sync → send edit → receive broadcast\n- [x] Verify final content via REST matches expected\n\n### 6.2 Concurrent edits converge\n- [x] Two clients edit same document simultaneously, both changes preserved\n- [x] Three clients, concurrent edits, all converge to same state\n- [x] Content is consistent after 10 simultaneous operations\n\n### 6.3 Persistence\n- [x] Server restart (stop/start) preserves documents on disk\n\n## Verification Steps\n1. `npm run build` compiles without errors\n2. `npm run lint` passes\n3. `npm test` passes all tests\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":60,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":33024,"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e3b5729a-6624-4d81-bb97-5a2094b26765","uuid":"c45a53db-fe5f-45c1-9cfb-e7d4572a4f1b"}
